  "research_note": "T-3566 (the owner, 2026-11-12, after a meeting with Bill Tyre): the frame house behind 1721's brick front should be standing, built to a photographic match of its south front in the Detroit print of the Pullman house (det 4a08065; the owner's crop of its left edge): two gabled wings, each a two-storey canted bay, either side of a recessed middle with the porch and front door, a shuttered window over the porch, bracketed eaves and tall stacks; symmetrical (the owner). Read through the Pullman house's solved camera on the print; Robinson's 1886 plate draws the house's south side stepped. Liberty L-k16-1721-frame-house-3566. Research note docs/RESEARCH/k16-1721-frame-house-3566/README.md.",
